WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.520
Big claws.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.859
Gnarly horns.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.860
Blood.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.620
Guts.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.040
Lion vs. lion.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.220
Elephant vs. elephant.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.020
A ferocious conflict that usually ends in death

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.400
for one or both of the individuals involved.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.760
That’s how we think most animal fights

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.360
go down in the wild.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.760
But the reality is that nature’s array of

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.680
weapons and conflicts are much more varied.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.280
Sometimes what appear to be deadly altercations

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.680
are actually just tests of strength.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.700
When members of the same species clash in the wild

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.660
over resources or a prospective mate,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.200
it doesn’t always go down how you think it will.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.240
[music]

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:51.060
First off, “to the death” isn’t the only option.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.700
Backing off can be the smarter move.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.240
Beadlet sea anemones sometimes escalate a situation,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.240
or sometimes they don’t.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.660
Observe as a sea anemone inflates its stinging tentacles

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.660
at a neighbor until it decides

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.480
enough is enough.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.420
It’s more exciting if you speed it up.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.820
Achieving victory doesn’t require blood.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.820
A caribbean rock mantis shrimp

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.860
uses club-like appendages

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.540
to bludgeon an opponent in the backside.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.900
Luckily, the shrimp’s rump

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.660
is also equipped with a shield.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.000
Eventually, someone gives up.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.320
The prize?

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.560
A burrow in a laboratory tank.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.060
Sometimes animals just need to

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.620
knock the other guy off his game.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.220
Rhinoceros beetles look scary

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.460
but rarely inflict serious damage.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.760
On a hot muggy night in Taiwan,

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.380
males vie for a female’s attention.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.660
On guard!

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.240
Using two pronged horns,

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.980
competitors fling each other from branches.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.060
The falls aren’t fatal.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.900
But to the victor go the spoils.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.980
Finally, ruthless killers are rare,

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.160
but they can be scarier than they look.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.080
These members of a species of nematode worms

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.320
resemble dueling spaghetti noodles

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.460
when they wrestle.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.720
But never go in against a nematode

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.720
when death is on the line.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.480
Given the right grip, they’ll squeeze

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.860
an opponent’s body until paralysis ensues.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.180
The loser slowly expires from internal injuries.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.200
In the animal kingdom,

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.880
it’s not always you win or you die,

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.520
but when it is, the arena is often tiny

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.600
and the conditions are cutthroat.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.940
[music]

